# DECC$SHR_EV56.vec -- OVMX's DECC$SHR_EV56.EXE, the C RTL image an image
# LINKed on real OpenVMS Alpha reaches when it calls DECC$SHR (rd vms-3b3f).
# SINGLE SOURCE for this image's symbol vector; format as in
# SYS$PUBLIC_VECTORS.vec.
#
# On OpenVMS Alpha the system logical DECC$SHR is "SYS$SHARE:DECC$SHR_EV56"
# (observed on the lab V8.4 node), so the activator opens this image for an
# image's DECC$SHR references. OVMX seeds the same logical
# (src/vmslnm/lnm_defaults.c, Alpha only). OVMX's own images name
# DECC$SHR.EXE, OVMX's C RTL, directly; this image forwards into it.
#
# Offsets are OBSERVED: the values our probe's link map reported
# (tools/lab-alpha/probes/ORDSC.MAR; docs/oracle/alpha84-symvec-offsets.txt,
# DECC$SHR rows). An entry is listed only where the OVMX routine takes the
# same arguments the way a 32-bit-pointer DEC C caller passes them (values and
# P0 string addresses) and returns a value, not a structure or pointer the
# caller would read in VMS layout. Every other slot is retired, so an image
# that calls one fails to activate (%IMGACT-I-NOTIMPL).
#
# DECC$TXPRINTF is printf with IEEE T_float doubles; OVMX's decc$tprintf is
# the same format engine. OVMX has no 128-bit X_float long double, so a
# %Lf argument is not supported (the register records it).
#
# GSMATCH: images linked on V8.4 record DECC$SHR ident major 1, minor 1,
# match LEQUAL (observed), so this image carries 1,1.
#
#   gsmatch LEQUAL,1,1
#   use     DECC$SHR.EXE
#
# offset  universal        OVMX target
0x1770    DECC$PUTCHAR     decc$putchar
0x1780    DECC$PUTS        decc$puts
0x2070    DECC$ABS         decc$abs
0x2080    DECC$ATOI        decc$atoi
0x26C0    DECC$STRCMP      decc$strcmp
0x2710    DECC$STRLEN      decc$strlen
0x4960    DECC$TXPRINTF    decc$tprintf
